From 12f8852228c9d8db58de90a2c086a7e182c4daf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:38:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] power: supply: apple_tristar: camera adapter to USB host,
 as iOS does

On iOS the camera adapter's DigitalID (11 f0 00 00 00 00) leads within
about 1 s to configureUSBMode(2) through IOAccessoryManagerUserClient
selector 1. The power handshake follows, and the adapter then provides
2100 mA at 5 V while the iPad is the host. There is no device-mode or
iAP phase.

Add that path as an accessory policy (apple_tristar_auto.h, pure
decisions shared with an offline harness), run from the existing 250 ms
supplier poll:

- GetID, without reorient, 300 ms after a plug edge and then every 2 s
  while no USB host uses the gadget (10 s while one does). It runs quietly:
  only ID and phase changes are logged.
- For 11 f0: the 0x72/0x70 power handshake (two tries; iOS enumerated
  the hub before its handshake finished, so host mode does not wait for
  it), then a claimed host role through the role switch.
- The host role lasts while the adapter is present. Three consecutive
  empty 0x0c reads (750 ms) or a different ID at the 5 s re-check return
  the port to device mode, and the gadget rebinds. If the user sets the
  role, the policy leaves it alone until the next unplug.
- While the adapter is identified, the supplier reports an online ACA
  source whenever VBUS is present, in host mode too: 500 mA before the
  handshake, then auto_input_ua (default and maximum 2100000, iOS's
  value). The input is never reported offline across the role switch.

auto_host=0 turns the policy off. The manual debugfs identify, handshake
and recover interfaces are unchanged; allow_power_handshake still gates
only the debugfs handshake. A world-readable lightning_state sysfs file
shows the phase, role, ID, handshake, supply, charger and battery state.
Debugfs auto_log keeps the last transitions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
